       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) lists a maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A 50 mg dose is well above that, so I can't treat it as within label limits. I'd rather not enter it as written when the risk is severe hypotension or shock.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n- **Enter a labeled dose:** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now. Just tell me which.\n- **Go ahead with 50 mg anyway:** If you have a specific clinical reason, the order should go through pharmacy review or a physician override in your institution's process. I can't make that decision for you. I can enter it with a note, such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max. Verified with pharmacy, rationale: ___\", once it has been cleared that way.\n- **Check the source:** If you're reading the 50 mg figure from a reference, please look at it again. It may be a different drug or a different formulation.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
